From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Mower <mdmower@cmphys.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 08:11:15 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [bugs #2970] sdas: open the .lst, .rel, and .sym files in
 binary mode again

In r12963 the mode for the output files of the assemblers was changed to "wb" for this ticket, so that a Windows host writes LF line endings. sdar does not find the symbols of a .rel file that has CRLF line endings and debug information. With the changes merged from upstream ASxxxx in r16921, afile() opened files of write code 1 with "w" again, and main() passes that code for the .lst, .rel, and .sym files.

afile() uses "wb" for write code 1 again, and the line is marked as specific to sdas. The change has no effect on a POSIX host. It was not tested on a Windows host.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sdas/asxxsrc/asmain.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sdas/asxxsrc/asmain.c b/sdas/asxxsrc/asmain.c
index cc3ca023e..4fede1f7b 100644
--- a/sdas/asxxsrc/asmain.c
+++ b/sdas/asxxsrc/asmain.c
@@ -2883,7 +2883,13 @@ afile(char *fs, char *ft, int wf)
 	switch(wf & 3) {
 	default:
 	case 0:	frmt = "r";	break;
-	case 1:	frmt = "w";	break;
+        /* sdas specific */
+        /* With "wb" the C library writes LF line endings on every host.
+         * sdar does not find the symbols of a .rel file that has CRLF
+         * line endings and debug information (bug #2970).
+         */
+        case 1: frmt = "wb";    break;
+        /* end sdas specific */
 	case 2:	frmt = "rb";	break;
 	case 3:	frmt = "wb";	break;
 	}
